  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>Nanobagrus armatus (Vaillant, 1902). Synonyms: Akysis armatus, Leiocassis armatus, Nannobagrus armatus. Type locality: Tepoe, Mahakam River, Borneo. Maximum size 32 mm (1.3\") SL.</p><p>The bagrid catfish genus Nanobagrus is found throughout Sundaic Southeast Asia. Members of the genus are diagnosed from other bagrid catfishes by their miniature adult size (maximum size under ca 45 mm SL), reduced supraoccipital process, reduced anterior nuchal-plate element, and a large and prominent posterior cranial fontanel. Its members typically inhabit small, forested streams with a moderate current. This species is easily distinguished by its small size and distinctive color pattern.</p><p>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2019).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>Asia: east and west Borneo. Pacific, Greater Sunda Island Rivers, Borneo waters.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>pH: 4.8 - 6.6.</p><p>Temperature: 22.0-27.0°C (71.6-80.6°F).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>Provide plenty of driftwood as hiding places.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>Readily feeds on live/frozen foods and other prepared foods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>A peaceful, shoaling species. Because of its small size, best kept with other very small fishes (e.g. Boraras) or in a species tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1003",
      "html": "<p>Males have an elongate genital papilla in front of the anal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
